# Wave W17-Y (Lake Gallant): gallant sand — the shore road’s pale sand, design-authorised: a clean pale sand running the lake’s rim from the Fenland road to the Brightshore road, washed bright by the open water beside it (design: the shore road ringing the lake under its lights). Split from Route 213’s salt-greyed sand by the wash entire and from Route 222’s beach sand ahead by the rim: this sand serves a lake, that one a sea beach.
